{#- modules/identity/oauth-to-aauth.j2
    One architecture diagram that turns itself from OAuth 2.1 into AAuth, one key
    press at a time. The parties stay where they are; labels, arrows and one badge
    change in place, so the eye tracks WHAT moved rather than re-reading a new slide.

      press 0  OAuth 2.1 authorization code: Person, Client, Resource Server,
               Identity Provider, Authorization Server. Bearer token.
      press 1  DPoP (RFC 9449): the token is bound to a key the client holds.
      press 2  AAuth agent identity: the agent_token binds a stable identifier to
               the agent's signing key (§5.2). Agent Provider appears; the
               resource verifies against the AP's JWKS, no pre-registration (§1.1, §5.1).
      press 3  PS authorization (three-party): the authorization server's consent
               job slides to the person's side, a Person Server. The resource
               answers 401 + AAuth-Requirement with a resource_token describing
               the access it needs (§3, §6.5); the agent trades it at the PS for an
               auth_token (§7.2); the PS handles consent (§7.2, 202 interaction).
      press 4  Federated (four-party): the resource delegates policy to an Access
               Server (§3). The resource_token's aud names the AS; the PS finds it
               at {aud}/.well-known/aauth-access.json and the AS returns the
               auth_token via the PS (§4.2.5, §9.3). The resource verifies via
               {iss}/.well-known/aauth-access.json → jwks_uri (§9.4.3, §11.5.2).

    Sources: draft-hardt-oauth-aauth-protocol-11 (25 Sept 2026, an individual IETF
    Internet-Draft, not a standard) for parties and tokens; aauth.dev for the tile
    names; RFC 9449 for DPoP; draft-ietf-oauth-v2-1-16 for the baseline.

    Machinery (pictograms, stage CSS, clickable crumbs, print) lives in morph-kit.j2.
    Primitive-native: import WITH CONTEXT.
      {%- from "modules/identity/oauth-to-aauth.j2" import morph with context %}
-#}

{%- from "modules/branding/" ~ branding ~ "/primitives.j2" import
    content_slide, slide_heading, card_grid, callout
-%}
{%- from "modules/identity/morph-kit.j2" import picto, glyph, sentinels, crumbs, styles -%}

{%- macro morph() -%}
{%- call content_slide("OAuth to AAuth") %}
{{ styles("o2a", 5, moves=[
  {"cls": "o2a-consent", "from": "translate(1412px, 134px)", "at": 3, "to": "translate(305px, 106px)"},
]) }}
<div class="o2a" style="position:relative;">
  {{ sentinels("o2a", 5) }}
  {{ slide_heading("", "From OAuth to AAuth, one change at a time") }}
  {{ crumbs("o2a", ["OAuth 2.1", "+ DPoP", "Identity Based", "Person Server Managed", "Federated"]) }}

  <svg viewBox="0 -15 1600 665" role="img"
       aria-label="Architecture diagram that steps from OAuth 2.1 to AAuth: a client becomes an agent with its own key, the authorization server's consent moves to a Person Server, and the resource keeps an Access Server.">
    <defs>
      <marker id="o2a-ah" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" fill="context-stroke"/>
      </marker>
    </defs>

    {#- ── arrows (under the parties) ─────────────────────────────── -#}

    {#- Person ↕ IdP / Person Server -#}
    <g class="mk-arrow o2a-v on0 on1 on3 on4 hot3">
      <path d="M250,240 L250,440" marker-start="url(#o2a-ah)" marker-end="url(#o2a-ah)"/>
      <text class="o2a-v on0 on1" x="264" y="346">signs in</text>
      <text class="o2a-v on3 on4" x="264" y="346">consents, in the moment</text>
    </g>

    {#- IdP → Authorization Server -#}
    <g class="mk-arrow o2a-v on0 on1">
      <path d="M299,120 L1291,120" marker-end="url(#o2a-ah)"/>
      <text x="800" y="104" text-anchor="middle">the person&rsquo;s identity</text>
    </g>

    {#- Client ↔ Authorization Server -#}
    <g class="mk-arrow o2a-v on0 on1 hot1">
      <path d="M812,447 L1291,140" marker-start="url(#o2a-ah)" marker-end="url(#o2a-ah)"/>
      <text class="o2a-v on0" x="1010" y="302" text-anchor="end">consent, code &#8644; Bearer token</text>
      <text class="o2a-v on1" x="1010" y="290" text-anchor="end">consent, code &#8644; token</text>
      <text class="o2a-v on1" x="1010" y="314" text-anchor="end">bound to the key (cnf.jkt)</text>
    </g>

    {#- Resource → Authorization Server -#}
    <g class="mk-arrow o2a-v on0 on1">
      <path d="M1350,240 L1350,440" marker-end="url(#o2a-ah)"/>
      <text x="1364" y="346">validates</text>
    </g>

    {#- Agent Provider → Agent -#}
    <g class="mk-arrow o2a-v on2 on3 on4 hot2">
      <path d="M760,240 L760,440" marker-end="url(#o2a-ah)"/>
      <text x="774" y="346">agent_token, bound to its key</text>
    </g>

    {#- Agent ↔ Person Server -#}
    <g class="mk-arrow o2a-v on3 on4 hot3">
      <path d="M722,447 L298,150" marker-start="url(#o2a-ah)" marker-end="url(#o2a-ah)"/>
      <text x="576" y="332">resource_token &#8644;</text>
      <text x="612" y="358">auth_token</text>
    </g>

    {#- Person Server ↔ Access Server, arcing over the Agent Provider -#}
    <g class="mk-arrow o2a-v on4 hot4">
      <path d="M298,78 C298,-20 1306,-20 1306,74" marker-start="url(#o2a-ah)" marker-end="url(#o2a-ah)"/>
      <text x="800" y="44" text-anchor="middle">resource_token &#8644; auth_token &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; the AS is named by the token&rsquo;s aud, found via its metadata</text>
    </g>

    {#- Client / Agent → Resource: the call itself -#}
    <g class="mk-arrow o2a-v on0 on1 on2 on3 on4 bad0 hot1 hot2 hot3">
      <path d="M818,482 L1296,482" marker-end="url(#o2a-ah)"/>
      <text class="o2a-v on0" x="1057" y="466" text-anchor="middle">Bearer token</text>
      <text class="o2a-v on1" x="1057" y="466" text-anchor="middle">token + fresh DPoP proof</text>
      <text class="o2a-v on2" x="1057" y="466" text-anchor="middle">HTTP signature + agent_token</text>
      <text class="o2a-v on3 on4" x="1057" y="466" text-anchor="middle">HTTP signature + auth_token</text>
    </g>

    {#- Resource → Agent: the 401 with a resource_token -#}
    <g class="mk-arrow o2a-v on3 on4 hot3 hot4">
      <path d="M1296,520 L820,520" marker-end="url(#o2a-ah)"/>
      <text class="o2a-v on3" x="1057" y="548" text-anchor="middle">401 + resource_token: the access it needs</text>
      <text class="o2a-v on4" x="1057" y="548" text-anchor="middle">401 + resource_token, for the Access Server</text>
    </g>

    {#- ── parties ────────────────────────────────────────────────── -#}

    <g class="mk-party side-p dim2" transform="translate(250,500)">
      {{ picto("person") }}
      <text class="t" y="85">Person</text>
      <text class="s o2a-v on0 on1 on2" y="108">the resource owner</text>
      <text class="s o2a-v on3 on4" y="108">accountable for the agent</text>
    </g>

    {#- The client is an IDE; from press 2 an agent lives in it -#}
    <g class="mk-party side-a hot1 hot2" transform="translate(760,500)">
      {{ picto("ide") }}
      {{ glyph("agent", 28, 26, 1.4, "ic o2a-v on2 on3 on4") }}
      <text class="t o2a-v on0 on1" y="85">Client</text>
      <text class="t o2a-v on2 on3 on4" y="85">Agent</text>
      <text class="s o2a-v on0" y="108">a client_id, registered at the AS</text>
      <text class="s o2a-v on1" y="108">a client_id, plus a private key</text>
      <text class="s o2a-v on2 on3 on4" y="108">an identifier bound to its key</text>
      <g class="mk-tag o2a-v on1 on2 on3 on4 hot1" transform="translate(-125,18)">
        <rect width="110" height="24" rx="12"/>
        <text x="55" y="16.5" text-anchor="middle">private key</text>
      </g>
    </g>

    <g class="mk-party side-r" transform="translate(1350,500)">
      {{ picto("rack") }}
      <text class="t o2a-v on0 on1" y="85">Resource Server</text>
      <text class="t o2a-v on2 on3 on4" y="85">Resource</text>
      <text class="s o2a-v on0" y="108">accepts whoever holds the token</text>
      <text class="s o2a-v on1" y="108">checks the proof matches the key</text>
      <text class="s o2a-v on2" y="108">verifies the signature, no registry</text>
      <text class="s o2a-v on3" y="108">describes the access it needs</text>
      <text class="s o2a-v on4" y="108">delegates policy to its Access Server</text>
    </g>

    <g class="mk-party side-p dim2 hot3" transform="translate(250,120)">
      {{ picto("badge") }}
      <text class="t o2a-v on0 on1 on2" y="85">Identity Provider</text>
      <text class="t o2a-v on3 on4" y="85">Person Server</text>
      <text class="s o2a-v on0 on1 on2" y="108">authenticates the person</text>
      <text class="s o2a-v on3 on4" y="108">speaks for the person</text>
    </g>

    <g class="mk-party side-a o2a-v on2 on3 on4 hot2" transform="translate(760,120)">
      {{ picto("key") }}
      <text class="t" y="85">Agent Provider</text>
      <text class="s" y="108">vouches for the agent&rsquo;s key</text>
    </g>

    {#- A login form while it is an OAuth authorization server; a policy
        clipboard once it is an AAuth Access Server -#}
    <g class="mk-party side-r dim2 dim3 hot4" transform="translate(1350,120)">
      {{ picto("login", "o2a-v on0 on1 on2") }}
      {{ picto("clipboard", "o2a-v on3 on4") }}
      <text class="t o2a-v on0 on1 on2" y="85">Authorization Server</text>
      <text class="t o2a-v on3 on4" y="85">Access Server</text>
      <text class="s o2a-v on0 on1 on2" y="108">the resource&rsquo;s: consent + tokens</text>
      <text class="s o2a-v on3" y="108">none in this mode</text>
      <text class="s o2a-v on4" y="108">the resource&rsquo;s policy engine</text>
      <g class="mk-tag hot4" transform="translate(62,-14)">
        <rect width="90" height="24" rx="12"/>
        <text x="45" y="16.5" text-anchor="middle">policy</text>
      </g>
    </g>

    {#- The consent badge: beside the Authorization Server until press 3, then
        it slides across to the Person Server. That slide IS the split. -#}
    <g class="mk-tag o2a-consent dim2 hot3">
      <rect width="100" height="24" rx="12"/>
      <text x="50" y="16.5" text-anchor="middle">consent</text>
    </g>
  </svg>
</div>
{%- endcall %}
{%- endmacro -%}


{%- macro other_modes() -%}
{%- call content_slide("AAuth other modes") %}
  {{ slide_heading("", "The modes in between, and the one past the end") }}
  {{ card_grid([
    {"title": "Resource managed",
     "body": "The resource runs the OAuth stack it already has and hands back a session token bound to the agent&rsquo;s signature. The bridge for a service that will not rewrite its auth.",
     "accent": "info"},
    {"title": "Person identity",
     "body": "The Person Server issues a <code>person_token</code> for one resource, and the resource decides on its own, as it would for a person who logged in. Federated login for agents.",
     "accent": "primary"},
    {"title": "Chained calls",
     "body": "A resource that calls onward signs the downstream request with its <em>own</em> key and passes the token it was handed as evidence of who it acts for. There is deliberately no delegation-chain claim.",
     "accent": "success"},
    {"title": "Per-call (R3, exploratory)",
     "body": "Rich Resource Requests: per-call proposals, authorized one call at a time. It governs a single action rather than a class of access.",
     "accent": "warning"},
  ], cols=2) }}
  {{ callout("Each mode adds one party. Identity-based replaces an API key this afternoon; add a Person Server when a person has to be answerable for the agent.", accent="primary") }}
  <p style="margin-top:1rem; text-align:center; font-size:0.85em; color:var(--slide-ink-3);">
    <a href="https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/draft-hardt-oauth-aauth-protocol" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="text-decoration:underline;">draft-hardt-oauth-aauth-protocol-11</a> (September 2026, an Internet-Draft) &middot; mode names from <a href="https://www.aauth.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="text-decoration:underline;">aauth.dev</a>
  </p>
{%- endcall %}
{%- endmacro -%}
